VALUES (
  'a9dacd89-0bec-5ffa-bf01-5c3875d85ba5', 'bce3226a-de1e-5ea2-b32d-9d3edab29bae',
  'Given `val` is the value of node (non-negative integer), `left` and `right` are the pointers to the left node and right node of it, respectively. Implement function:

```cpp
int longestPathSum(BTNode* root);
```

where `root` is the root node of given binary tree (this tree has between 1 and 100000 elements). This function returns the sum of the largest path from the root node to a leaf node. If there are more than one equally long paths, return the larger sum.

Example: Given a binary tree in the following:

[Tree Diagram: Root 1 -> Left 5, Right 4. Node 4 -> Left 7, Right 12. Node 7 -> Left 4, Right 8. Node 4 (child of 7) -> Left 2.]

The longest path from the root node to the leaf node is `1-4-7-4-2`, so return the sum of this path, is `18`.

Note: In this exercise, the libraries `iostream`, `utility`, `queue`, `stack` and `using namespace std` are used. You can write helper functions; however, you are not allowed to use other libraries.', 5
);

